    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shep95/aureon.defender/zipball/v0.4.1",
    "body": "Direct downloads, no app stores. Source and platform scope are in the repository README.\n\n- Windows x64 0.4.0: tested Windows engine and Signal dashboard. Extract the full ZIP. Unsigned publisher.\n- Android 0.4.1 APK: native local monitor and floating navigation. Android 12+; OS background limits apply.\n- iPhone/iPad: https://shep95.github.io/aureon.defender/ \u2014 Safari > Share > Add to Home Screen. This is a web edition, not a native IPA or system antivirus. The web-edition ZIP is for HTTPS self-hosting.\n- macOS/Linux: any attached native packages are limited portable PREVIEWS. They do not contain the full Windows engine. Native CI tests and packaged-executable smoke checks run before upload. Mac packages are not Developer ID signed or notarized; Linux compatibility depends on distribution/architecture.\n- Portable Python source is also attached. No country geofence is implemented; worldwide OS/network/store-independent availability is not guaranteed.\n\nVerification: Windows 101 tests (1 phone test skipped), 15 live dashboard pages and 45 responsive page checks; Android 10 rule/file assertions and 19 Pixel checks; web known-answer hashing, invalid imports, report text rendering and offline-cache reload. No multi-day endurance or every-device guarantee. Check SHA256SUMS.txt; each CI-built preview has its own .sha256 file.\n\nNo API keys, signing keys, personal runtime histories or passwords are included. Third-party notices remain applicable. Three Windows abuse.ch feeds need a user-provided API key. This release grants no new platform privileges or patent clearance.\n\n\n## Current distribution status\nWindows and Android downloads are attached and verified. Store-free iPhone/iPad web edition: https://aureon-defender.vercel.app/ (Safari: Share \u2192 Add to Home Screen; local file/hash and report tools only, not a native IPA or background antivirus).\n\nNative Mac/Linux packages are **not available**: GitHub stopped every hosted build before execution because the account is locked due to a billing issue. The portable source preview and build workflow are included; no native build/test success is claimed.\n"
